record.statement:
For the Robin Laplacian with positive boundary parameter $\alpha$, given positive numbers $\alpha$ and $M$, do there exist positive constants $a$ and $b$, depending only on $\alpha$, $M$, and $n$, such that, for every $k\in\mathbb N$ and every domain $\Omega$ with $|\Omega|=M$,

- $\rho_k(\Omega)\ge a k^{2/(2n-1)}$ when $\Omega$ is convex;
- $\rho_k(\Omega)\ge b k^{1/n}$ for general $\Omega$?
